     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg per day. That is twice the maximum prescription dose of 3,200 mg per day for adults. Typical doses are 400\u2013800 mg per dose, up to four times daily. A dose this high greatly raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You've said you're a financial analyst and not a clinician. Orders should be placed by the treating clinician, or entered at their direction and verified by pharmacy.\n\nIf this came from a clinician, it may be a typo. For example, they may have meant 1600 mg total per day, or 400 mg or 800 mg per dose. Please ask them to confirm the intended order. If they want to enter it themselves, or send me a corrected dose, I can help from there."
      }
     ],
