     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg per day is twice the 3,200 mg daily maximum. You confirmed the order as written, but that doesn't make the dose safe for the patient.\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** The confirmation needs to come from the treating clinician, not from someone in the finance office.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating clinician to review the order. They can enter it themselves or tell me the intended dose.\n- If the clinician really intends a dose above the maximum, pharmacy should review it. It would need documented clinical justification.\n- If it was a typo, send me the corrected dose, such as 400 mg or 800 mg every 6\u20138 hours. The order would still need to come from, or be verified by, the prescriber.\n\nI can enter an order as soon as I have a safe dose that a prescriber has confirmed."
      }
     ],
